<mjml>
  <mj-head>
    <mj-attributes>
      <mj-all padding="0" />
      <mj-text font-family="sans-serif" />
      <mj-class name="header" padding="10px 10px 20px 10px" background-color="white" />
      <mj-class name="header-title" align="left" font-family="monospace" font-size="24pt" font-weight="600" line-height="24pt" padding-bottom="10px" />
      <mj-class name="header-image" align="right" width="100px" />
      <mj-class name="header-issue" align="left" font-family="monospace" font-weight="200" />
      <mj-class name="header-date" align="right" font-family="monospace" font-weight="200" />

      <mj-class name="article" padding-bottom="10px" />
      <mj-class name="article-title" font-family="monospace" font-weight="400" font-size="14pt" />

      <mj-class name="summary" padding="0 10px 20px 10px" />

      <mj-class name="category-heading" font-family="monospace" font-weight="600" font-size="18pt" />

      <mj-class name="articles" padding="0 10px 0 10px" />
      <mj-class name="images" padding="0 10px 20px 10px" />

      <mj-class name="footer" padding="10px 10px 10px 10px" />

      <mj-class name="footer-unsub" align="left" />
      <mj-class name="footer-feedback" align="right" />
    </mj-attributes>
  </mj-head>
  <mj-body>
    <mj-container>

      <!-- Header -->
      <mj-wrapper mj-class="header">
        <mj-section>
          <mj-column width="100%" vertical-align="middle">
            <mj-text mj-class="header-title">Newsletter del Lunes.</mj-text>
          </mj-column>
        </mj-section>

        <mj-section>
          <mj-group>
            <mj-column width="50%">
              <mj-text mj-class="header-issue">Issue No. 35</mj-text>
            </mj-column>
            <mj-column width="50%">
              <mj-text mj-class="header-date">28 Julio 2025</mj-text>
            </mj-column>
          </mj-group>
        </mj-section>

        <mj-section>
          <mj-column>
            <mj-divider border-width="1px" border-style="dotted" border-color="lightgrey" />
          </mj-column>
        </mj-section>
      </mj-wrapper>
      <!-- /Header -->

      <!-- Summary -->
      <mj-section mj-class="summary">
        <mj-column>
          <mj-text>
            
Buenas a todos,
</br></br>
En esta edición tenemos un especial de Systemd, el gran sistema de arranque de casi todos los SO Linux modernos. Además de un poquito de C++ y un poquito de Python.
</br></br>
Comentar que ya no vuelvo a enviar nada hasta septiembre. Tambin comento que los que no quieran seguir recibiendo el correo que me lo notifique, que juro que no habrá represalias...
</br></br>
Un saludo!

          </mj-text>
        </mj-column>
      </mj-section>

      <!-- Images -->
      <mj-section mj-class="images">
        <mj-column>
          
        </mj-column>
      </mj-section>
      
      <mj-section>
        <mj-column>
          <mj-text>
            <h2>Artículos</h2>
          </mj-text>
        </mj-column>
      </mj-section>

      <!-- Articles -->
			<mj-wrapper mj-class="articles">
				
          
					<mj-section mj-class="article">
						<mj-column>
							
              <mj-text mj-class="article-title"><a href="https://medium.com/@obaff/how-to-structure-a-systemd-service-file-8fa8ab758947">How to Structure a systemd Service File | by Obafemi | Jul, 2025 | Medium</a></mj-text>
              
							<mj-text mj-class="article-summary">Como estructurar un servicio en systemd, es básico pero completo, en la documentación oficial te puedes perder.</mj-text>
						</mj-column>
					</mj-section>
				  
        
          
					<mj-section mj-class="article">
						<mj-column>
							
              <mj-text mj-class="article-title"><a href="https://medium.com/@obaff/11-systemctl-commands-for-power-users-in-production-a90db1cf30a7">11 systemctl Commands for Power Users in Production | by Obafemi | Jul, 2025 | Medium</a></mj-text>
              
							<mj-text mj-class="article-summary">Comandos para hacer cositas en systemd, útil saberlo para tener control sobre lo que ocurre en el sistema a nivel de servicios.</mj-text>
						</mj-column>
					</mj-section>
				  
        
          
					<mj-section mj-class="article">
						<mj-column>
							
              <mj-text mj-class="article-title"><a href="https://cppdoctor.com/blog/3-common-myths-about-c-lambdas">3 C++ Lambdas Myths</a></mj-text>
              
							<mj-text mj-class="article-summary">Texto cortito sobre Lambdas en C++, pero me pareció interesante.</mj-text>
						</mj-column>
					</mj-section>
				  
        
          
					<mj-section mj-class="article">
						<mj-column>
							
              <mj-text mj-class="article-title"><a href="https://blog.devgenius.io/pythons-vision-c-s-strength-the-art-of-delegating-computationally-demanding-challenges-to-c-00fc86f7fc6a">Python’s Vision, C++’s Strength: The Art of Delegating Computationally Demanding Challenges to C++ developed extensions. | by Masoud Masoumi Moghadam | Dev Genius</a></mj-text>
              
							<mj-text mj-class="article-summary">Y por último texto sobre python y compilaciones de funciones y código, puede que algún proyecto pueda salir beneficiado, o eso espero.</mj-text>
						</mj-column>
					</mj-section>
				  
        

        
      </mj-wrapper>

      <!-- Footer -->
      <mj-wrapper mj-class="footer">
        <mj-section>
          <mj-column>
            <mj-divider border-width="1px" border-style="dotted" border-color="lightgrey" padding-bottom="5px" />
          </mj-column>
        </mj-section>

        <mj-section>
          <mj-group>
            <mj-column width="50%">
              <mj-text mj-class="footer-unsub">Not interested? <a href="mailto:daniel.agredano@gtd.eu?Subject=iX%20Newsletter%20--%20Unsubscribe">Unsubscribe</a></mj-text>
            </mj-column>
            <mj-column width="50%">
              <mj-text mj-class="footer-feedback"><a href="mailto:daniel.agredano@gtd.eu?Subject=iX%20Newsletter%20--%20Feedback">Feedback</a></mj-text>
            </mj-column>
          </mj-group>
        </mj-section>
      </mj-wrapper>

    </mj-container>
  </mj-body>
</mjml>
